          {
            "locale": "zh",
            "day": 1,
            "markers": 0,
            "text": "D1 浅草历史文化与小食\nTokyo\n尚无已确认位置，请先补全地点；日程仍可正常查看。\n地图尚未接入，先按下方顺序游览\n1\n上午\n浅草寺与仲见世商店街\n浅草寺是东京最具代表性的文化地标，拥有约1400年历史。寺前的仲见世商店街长约200米，两旁店铺售卖各种纪念品和本地小吃，是感受江户风情与品尝小吃的绝佳去处。\n尚未确认具体位置\n2\n下午\n东京街头小吃：拉面、章鱼烧、鲷鱼烧等\n东京街头小吃种类繁多，从拉面、章鱼烧到鲷鱼烧、御好烧、烧鸟等，遍布各处摊位和店铺，是体验当地饮食文化的直接方式。\n尚未确认具体位置\n在规划记录中调整\n上午、下午等为建议游览时段。"
          },
          {
            "locale": "zh",
            "day": 2,
            "markers": 1,
            "text": "D2 明治神宫与本地食文化\nTokyo\n1\n明治神宫\n+\n−\n Leaflet | © OpenStreetMap contributors\n游览顺序示意 · 非导航路线\n地图仅显示已有坐标的地点\n1\n上午\n明治神宫\n明治神宫是东京重要的传统神社，环境宁静，适合在清晨或上午安静地参访，感受日本神道文化。\n已确认场馆位置\n2\n下午\n东京本地特色：文字烧与深川饭\n文字烧是一种类似御好烧的咸味煎饼，深川饭是蛤蜊盖饭，还有柳川锅等，都是东京独有的地方美食，值得一试。\n尚未确认具体位置\n在规划记录中调整\n上午、下午等为建议游览时段。"
          },
          {
            "locale": "en",
            "day": 1,
            "markers": 0,
            "text": "D1 Asakusa History and Street Food\nTokyo\nNo confirmed locations yet. Resolve places to add the map; the itinerary remains available.\nMap not connected yet. Follow the itinerary below.\n1\nMorning\nSensoji Temple and Nakamise Street\nStart your Tokyo visit in Asakusa at Sensoji Temple, a cultural landmark with about 1,400 years of history. After exploring the temple grounds, stroll along Nakamise Street, a traditional shopping street about 200 meters long, where you can sample local snacks and browse souvenirs.\nSpecific location not confirmed\n2\nAfternoon\nTokyo Street Food: Ramen, Takoyaki, Taiyaki\nSpend the afternoon exploring Tokyo's street food scene. Look for stalls and shops serving iconic treats like ramen, takoyaki (octopus balls), taiyaki (fish-shaped cakes), okonomiyaki (savory pancakes), and yakitori (grilled chicken skewers).\nSpecific location not confirmed\nAdjust in planning history\nMorning and afternoon are suggested visiting periods."
          },
          {
            "locale": "en",
            "day": 2,
            "markers": 1,
            "text": "D2 Meiji Shrine and Local Cuisine\nTokyo\n1\nMeiji Jingu Shrine\n+\n−\n Leaflet | © OpenStreetMap contributors\nVisit order · Not a navigation route\nOnly places with coordinates appear on the map.\n1\nMorning\nMeiji Jingu Shrine\nBegin your second day with a quiet visit to Meiji Jingu, one of Tokyo's major Shinto shrines. The serene forested grounds offer a peaceful contrast to the city's bustle, ideal for a calm morning stroll.\nConfirmed venue location\n2\nAfternoon\nTokyo Local Specialties: Monjayaki and Fukagawa Meshi\nIn the afternoon, try Tokyo's local specialties. Sample monjayaki, a savory pancake similar to okonomiyaki, Fukagawa meshi (clam rice), and Yanagawa nabe hot pot, all classic dishes that showcase the city's culinary heritage.\nSpecific location not confirmed\nAdjust in planning history\nMorning and afternoon are suggested visiting periods."
          }
        ],
